From 7271eaf7776b67574c764f823c37b89154d5e945 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jose Drowne <jdrowne@10ulabs.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Dec 2025 14:30:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Inline small CFuncs to reduce function call overhead
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add --inline-cfuncs <threshold> option (0=disabled, default=20) to inline
small CFunc calls directly into their callers. This reduces function call
overhead when --output-split-cfuncs is used, since the C++ compiler cannot
inline across compilation units.

Creates V3InlineCfuncs pass that runs after V3Reloop. Functions are inlined
when they have <= threshold nodes, no local variables, no $c() statements,
void return type, and are in the same scope as the caller.

Adds V3Stats tracking: "Optimizations, Inlined CFuncs"

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
